Z||000000||sportscarguy||05-07-2001||06:55 PM||||I have an 85 4 cylinder 5 speed, the trans has started making a ticking noise at highway speed, the noise happens about every 3 second.  I can hear the ticking in both 4th and 5th gear. the frequency of the ticking does not seem to change under a change of load or speed, however when the clutch is depressed the noise goes away.  I also have a problem with it jumping out of reverse when backing up a grade, but it is fine on the level.<P>Any suggestions ?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||05-07-2001||07:12 PM||||Welcome to the board!  I've never heard of a ticking only in 4th and 5th.  Try changing the tranny fluid and look to see if there is anything that shouldn't be there in the oil.  When was the last time you changed the fluid?<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
